// Is the ticket's host one machine? Splits the host's records by the address
// that delivered them. A cloned or restored VM reports the original's Hostname
// until it is renamed, so one asset key can be two machines. One row is the
// normal answer; two or more rows are two or more machines — attribute every
// cited event to its Sender before judging it. A clone's record range starts
// inside the original's and stops below it. EventTime is host-local time.
// '@sender' must stay bracket-quoted: a bare @sender silently returns null.
// Placeholders: {HOST} = host name as the events spell it; {WFROM}/{WTO}.
WindowsAudit
| where timestamp between (datetime("{WFROM}") .. datetime("{WTO}"))
| where Hostname =~ "{HOST}"
| summarize events = count(),
            firstEvent = min(tostring(EventTime)), lastEvent = max(tostring(EventTime)),
            minRecord = min(RecordNumber), maxRecord = max(RecordNumber),
            lsassPids = make_set_if(ProcessID, EventID == 4624, 10)
    by Sender = tostring(['@sender'])
| order by events desc
| take 1000
